<title>UK: LME copper stable, zinc clings to fresh highs.</title>
<headline>LME copper stable, zinc clings to fresh highs.</headline>
<text>
<p>COPPER - Barely changed from Wednesday's sub-$2,600 kerb close. Spreads stay tights.</p>
<p>ZINC - Stronger after hitting fresh 4-3/4 year highs in pre-market.</p>
<p>ALUMINIUM  - Barely easier, reluctant to approach $1,600.</p>
<p>LEAD - Quiet, just firmer..</p>
<p>NICKEL - Softer, but above $7,200.  OTHERS - Slightly firmer.</p>
